<p>On November 14, 2026, <a href={dellStatement}>Michael Dell said</a> that over 90% of the 25 million accounts he and Susan Dell funded were still unclaimed. A separate count for that group has not been published.</p>
<p><a href={treasuryEnrollment}>Treasury enrolled about 60 million children automatically on October 1, 2026</a>. About 164,000 of those accounts were claimed in the first week, or about 0.3% of the auto-enrolled group. Treasury benefits tax counsel Helen Morrison gave that early count in her personal capacity at an American Bar Association tax meeting, as reported by <a href={reportedClaims}>Bloomberg Law</a> and cited by <a href={fortuneClaims}>Fortune on November 10</a>.</p>
